[high] internal/service/worker/service.go:331 (correctness vs. the actual SDK/library)
The dashboard suggestion worker is registered through river.WorkFunc, whose wrapper embeds River WorkerDefaults and does not consult DashboardSuggestionCellArgs.Timeout(). In River v0.30 the timeout must come from the Worker Timeout method or river.Config.JobTimeout, so this job inherits River default JobTimeout (1 minute) instead of the intended 5 minutes. That is shorter than the default AI request timeout (120s), and completeWithOneRetry can make two such calls, so normal slow LLM calls can be cancelled by River before the worker request timeout/retry policy completes; on the final attempt the failure-marking path then uses the cancelled job context and can leave the cell pending while River discards the job.
Suggested fix: Register a real DashboardSuggestionWorker that embeds river.WorkerDefaults[DashboardSuggestionCellArgs] and implements Timeout(*river.Job[DashboardSuggestionCellArgs]) time.Duration, then call river.AddWorker(workers, dashboardSuggestionWorker) instead of wrapping Work with river.WorkFunc. Size the timeout to cover the configured AI request timeout plus the in-job retry and DB work, or set an explicit river.Config.JobTimeout that safely covers this worker.
Guidance: Fix internal/service/worker/dashboard_suggestion_worker.go and internal/service/worker/service.go so River sees a worker-level timeout. In DashboardSuggestionWorker, embed river.WorkerDefaults[DashboardSuggestionCellArgs] in the struct and add func (w *DashboardSuggestionWorker) Timeout(job *river.Job[DashboardSuggestionCellArgs]) time.Duration. Do not rely on DashboardSuggestionCellArgs.Timeout(); River v0.30 calls Worker.Timeout(job), and river.WorkFunc wraps the Work method with WorkerDefaults whose Timeout returns 0. Size the timeout to cover two LLM calls plus DB work, for example compute requestTimeout from w.aiCfg.RequestTimeout or config.DefaultAIConfig().RequestTimeout, then return 2*requestTimeout plus a small buffer such as 30 seconds, with a floor of 5*time.Minute if you want to preserve the existing intended value. In internal/service/worker/service.go, replace river.AddWorker(workers, river.WorkFunc(dashboardSuggestionWorker.Work)) with river.AddWorker(workers, dashboardSuggestionWorker). Keep JobTypeDashboardSuggestionCell, DashboardSuggestionQueue, MaxAttempts, and ByArgs uniqueness unchanged. Add or adjust a unit test to assert DashboardSuggestionWorker.Timeout returns the expected duration from default/configured AI request timeout; the existing DashboardSuggestionCellArgs.Timeout test alone is insufficient because it does not exercise River's worker API.
